codex
The absent `Item` names are overwhelmingly split across existing item-stack data components and the live `ItemBehaviour`/item-use paths. I found one real callable gap while tracing `Item.use`/`getUseDuration`: the base vanilla path starts use for `KINETIC_WEAPON`, but both packet handlers only recognized consumables and shields, while Pumpkin’s stack duration also ignored that component. I’m wiring that existing component through both live handlers and removing the spear-only duplicate start so off-hand use follows the packet hand.
