crates/pumpkin-data/src/generated/translation.rs:73176:                "New Minecraft is the only place to receive future updates containing new features, mobs, items, blocks and much more!",
crates/pumpkin-data/src/generated/translation.rs:74487:                "Add-Ons are a content type available in the Minecraft Marketplace that lets you add custom blocks, items, mobs, recipes, and other game content to your world.",
crates/pumpkin-data/src/generated/translation.rs:74534:                "Armor can be crafted from Leather, Iron, Gold, or Diamond. Chainmail Armor can be obtained through villager trading and loot from zombies and skeletons.",
crates/pumpkin-data/src/generated/translation.rs:74623:                "They are crafted with Glass, Obsidian, and Nether Stars (which is obtained by defeating the Wither).",
crates/pumpkin-data/src/generated/translation.rs:74680:                "Most blocks you will have to find in the world, but some can only be crafted such as combining other blocks on a crafting table like a Redstone Block or smelted in a furnace like Glass.",
crates/pumpkin-data/src/generated/translation.rs:74697:                "§eTerracotta§f - This is found naturally in Badlands biomes or can be crafted and dyed from Clay that is found underwater. Terracotta can be made into Glazed Terracotta by smelting it in a Furnace.",
crates/pumpkin-data/src/generated/translation.rs:74778:                "Once you have crafted a Chest, you can place it in the world and then open it with :_input_key.use: to store items from your inventory.",
crates/pumpkin-data/src/generated/translation.rs:74781:                "Once you have crafted a Chest, you can place it in the world and then tap to open it and store items from your inventory.",
crates/pumpkin-data/src/generated/translation.rs:74845:                "A Conduit is crafted with Nautilus Shells and a Heart of the Sea. The Conduit draws power from Prismarine and Sea Lanterns.",
crates/pumpkin-data/src/generated/translation.rs:74857:                "§eTools§f help you get things done faster. Some, like the §epickaxe§f:wood_pickaxe: , let you mine stone and various ores. Others, like the §esword§f:wood_sword: , help you keep enemies at bay.",
crates/pumpkin-data/src/generated/translation.rs:74871:                "To place or use certain Minecraft Education blocks or items, a player must possess a special ability called 'World Builder'.",
crates/pumpkin-data/src/generated/translation.rs:74963:                "Students can simulate real world chemistry by using the Chemistry Equipment blocks. Build any of the 118 different elements by adjusting the sliders in the Element Constructor or view the composition of elements by placing them in the Element Constructor. Combine elements in the Compound Creator to produce chemical compounds. Put elements and compounds into the Lab Table to create Minecraft items. Reduce blocks to their component elements with the Material Reducer.",
crates/pumpkin-data/src/generated/translation.rs:75042:                "The creative mode interface allows any item in the game to be moved into the player's inventory without the need for mining or crafting the item. The items in the player's inventory will not be removed when they are placed or used in the world, and this allows the player to focus on building rather than resource gathering.",
crates/pumpkin-data/src/generated/translation.rs:75127:                "Some Dye materials are harder to find than others. Most Dyes can be crafted from flowers, like §eRed Dye§f from a Poppy, but some Dyes are found or created in more obscure ways such as:",
