The audit shows the remaining leads are mostly intentional API-name mismatches or data/components: tool rules, jukebox playability, rarity, pickaxe/nautilus properties, map post-processing, bundle overrides, and item destruction are already consumed through live Rust paths. I found one parity defect inside that existing bundle override path: it bypasses slot transfer callbacks/limits, unlike vanilla’s `safeTake`/`safeInsert`; I’m fixing that reachable path and adding evidence for it.
